# Mirrormind Crown: "the first time you would create one or more tokens each turn, you may instead create that many tokens
# that are copies of equipped creature." Turn 3: the Crown is on Llanowar Elves; Obsessive Pursuit enters and makes a Clue,
# the turn's first creation - Bot1 declines, so the Clue is made, and that used the turn's first time up. Turn 4: Bot2's
# Lingering Souls makes Spirits - not Bot1's tokens, so Bot1 is asked nothing. Turn 5: at upkeep Pursuit's Clue is the first
# creation and Bot1 takes the copy (an Elves token in place of the Clue, one for one); then Bot1's Lingering Souls, the turn's
# second creation, makes its two Spirits as written with no question.

